/*
 * The refgrid cell table: the one place that says what is drawn and where.
 * refgrid.c includes this file to build its cell array; grid-export.mjs parses it to write grid.json.
 *
 *   CELL(sheet, id, kind, x, y, w, h, a, b, state, text)
 *
 * sheet  1 = drawn with DrawEdge and DrawFrameControl, 2 = real child controls, 3 = top-level windows and the menu.
 * x y w h  pixels in the 640 by 480 grid window, which sits at the top left of the screen. They must be plain
 *          integers. Nothing may overlap the ready marker (x 0 to 39, y 0 to 7).
 * a, b   meaning depends on the kind; see the comment above each block.
 * state  ST_* flags applied by message after the control is created.
 * Edit by hand; keep one cell per line.
 */

/* Sheet 1. DrawEdge: one row per edge type, one column per flag set (BF_RECT is always added by the program). */
